Subject: [PATCH] Obfuscation detection

This patch implements advanced obfuscation detection capabilities for
Minecraft server plugins. It analyzes JAR files during plugin loading
to identify potentially obfuscated or malicious code by examining:
    - Class naming patterns (short names, sequential patterns, confusion)
    - Package structure anomalies
    - Encrypted strings and string decryption methods
    - Anti-debugging techniques
    - Excessive use of synthetic/bridge methods
    - Arithmetic and bitwise operation obfuscation
    - Cryptographic API usage patterns

The detection system uses configurable thresholds and multiple heuristics
to identify obfuscated plugins while minimizing false positives.

Author: GideonWhite1029
License: GPL-3.0 (https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-3.0.html)

